# UI and Theme Conventions

Read `docs/THEME_GUIDE.md` and `docs/UI_SYSTEMS.md` for full details.

## Painted Table theme

- **Paper or glass**: paper (`themes/generated/paper_theme.tres`) is the project default for
  anything that stops play; every UI root shown while play continues sets
  `ThemeColors.glass_theme()`. `tests/unit/test_glass_roots.gd` lists both kinds.
- **Colours**: roles from `ThemeColors` (`TEXT`, `TEXT_SOFT`, `ACCENT`, `STATE`, `DANGER` ...),
  read with `ThemeColors.of(control, role)` only when drawing by hand; never a `Color(` literal.
- **Buttons**: the default is the quiet secondary; `Primary` (one per screen), `Danger` (danger
  confirm only), `Ghost`, `IconButton`, `Tile`, `Card`.
- **Typography**: `Wordmark`, `Title`/`H1`, `Heading`/`H2`, `H3`, `Body` (the default),
  `Caption` (14, the floor), `BodyState`/`CaptionState`; Fraunces only for wordmark, titles,
  headings.
- **Panels**: the default PanelContainer is a `Sheet`; `Inset`, `KeyChip`, `Badge`.
- **Theme scripts**: `themes/painted_theme_base.gd` and its leaves; regenerate both with
  `tools/regen_theme.gd`.

## UI Primitives

Read `docs/THEME_GUIDE.md`'s "UI Primitives" and "Motion" sections. Compose these
(`scenes/ui/primitives/`) rather than raw Buttons and sliders:

- `IconButton` — icon-only actions, rail items, pane headers
- `IconRail` — one-of-N section choice (drawer rail, Settings sections)
- `TileRow` — enums with six or fewer options; multi-select toggles
- `Foldout` — advanced/secondary rows
- `PropertyRow` — label + optional check/colour + slider + inline value
- `PaneStack` — one-visible-pane content area with crossfade

Motion tokens (`Constants`): `ANIM_HOVER_IN`/`ANIM_HOVER_OUT`, `ANIM_PRESS`,
`ANIM_PANE_SWAP`/`ANIM_PANE_SWAP_OFFSET_PX`, `ANIM_FOLDOUT`.

## CanvasLayer Order

| Layer | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| 2 | AppMenu (persistent) |
| 10 | Pause overlay |
| 80–110 | UIManager components |

## Animated Panels

- Extend `AnimatedVisibilityContainer` for panels with show/hide animations.
- Implement `animate_in()` / `animate_out()` or `close()`.
- Use lifecycle callbacks: `_on_before_animate_in()`, `_on_after_animate_out()`.

## ESC Handling

Overlays that should close on ESC must:

1. Call `UIManager.register_overlay(self)` when shown.
2. Implement `animate_out()` or `close()`.
3. Call `UIManager.unregister_overlay(self)` when hidden.

## UIManager Quick Reference

```gdscript
UIManager.show_confirmation("Title", "Message")
UIManager.show_success("Saved!")
await UIManager.transition(func(): do_something())
UIManager.register_overlay(my_panel)
```
